  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 85ee28e4018ba2d4f96dec74f1af3a1e, type: 3}
  m_Name: Popup3_Handling
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TutorialPopup
  TutorialPages:
  - If a bear is approaching, you should <color=#cc5200>start spraying</color> when
    it comes within 9-12m (30-40ft) of your position.\n\n This is <color=#cc5200>
    about the length of a bus</color>.
  - Spray canisters hold limited supply! They will usually hold about 7-9 seconds
    worth of spray.
  - Unless a bear is charging, use <color=#cc5200>1-2 second bursts</color> to conserve
    supply. \nTry spraying the target.
  - Finally, ensure there are <color=#cc5200> no strong winds blowing towards your
    face</color>. You do not want to spray yourself instead of the bear!
  Step: 3
